38) and Hoseah TJALE (05:44:42). Helen LUCRE won the women's race in 06:48:42, followed by Lindsay WEIGHT (06:58:44).\n\nHelen LUCRE's 06:48:42 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nIn a remarkable coincidence, Bruce FORDYCE's winning time of 05:37:01 was identical to the second to the winning time posted in 1985 — both on the same direction course.\n\nFrom a field of 10,828 entries, 8,370 runners completed the course for a 77.3% finish rate. The field comprised 7,963 men and 407 women (4.9% female). The average finish time was 09:30:42.\n\nMedals awarded: 11 Gold, 704 Silver, 7,655 Bronze. 2,523 runners (30.1%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Leo MOSS in 10:59:58.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1985, the field was 7.3% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 21% of the finishers, with 6,602 seniors (avg 09:28:47) and 1,766 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.0}